#
# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the EverLive test suite.
#
# everlive_framestore is a lock-free seqlock.  The producer fills a private
# back slot and publishes it with release semantics; readers copy the published
# slot and then re-check the sequence number.  A producer that wraps can
# overwrite the slot a reader is copying, so the raw frame copies intentionally
# overlap.  everlive_framestore_read_snapshot() detects that overlap through
# everlive_framestore_read_validate() and retries, so this is a benign race that
# TSan cannot model.  Keep the suppression narrow to the two data-path
# functions.
race:everlive_framestore_publish
race:everlive_framestore_read_snapshot
